===== APEX_GEN5.md:18670-18690 (baseline) =====
 18670	
 18671	**Validation order (sequential, fail-fast):**
 18672	1. Schema conformance: all required fields present, correct types.
 18673	2. Finite numerics: no NaN/Inf in OHLCV; Decimal precision adequate.
 18674	3. OHLC bounds: O ≥ 0, H ≥ max(O, C), L ≤ min(O, C), H ≥ L, no swaps.
 18675	4. Volume and OI: non-negative; zero volume is permitted only for OPEN status; OI policy (AI.6).
 18676	5. UTC timestamp: valid ISO 8601 UTC format, millisecond precision.
 18677	6. Sequence check: strictly increasing for same symbol+timeframe; gap or reorder triggers correction event.
 18678	7. Duplicate detection: (symbol, timeframe, timestamp, open, close, volume) hash against recent ledger; exact match = duplicate; similar hash = potential out-of-order.
 18679	8. Closed-only rule: only CLOSED status candles enter the feature pipeline; OPEN/PARTIAL are buffered or rejected.
 18680	9. Availability and PIT check: timestamp <= as_of <= max(availability_time + settlement_lag); if violated, mark STALE (AI.6).
 18681	10. Source health: check provider status, connection latency, last-quote age; degraded sources are flagged as QX (AI.6).
 18682	
 18683	**Never swap H and L or silently replace missing values.** If H < L, reject the record and log error; if numeric value is missing, mark MISSING (AI.6), not zero.
 18684	
 18685	**Correction and immutability model:**
 18686	
 18687	Define three canonical statuses:
 18688	- **MISSING:** field value not yet available or not provided.
 18689	- **PARTIAL:** candle not yet closed; only open/high/low/volume are reliable.
 18690	- **CLOSED:** candle is immutable; open, high, low, close, volume, and OI (if provided) are final.

